{%- layout none -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Read by cc-cart.js.liquid to build the Checkout Champ `products=` list.

  The separator is driven by a `first` flag rather than `forloop.last`. Only
  items that carry the productId metafield are emitted, so `forloop.last` put a
  comma after the last EMITTED item whenever the last CART item was skipped —
  `[{...},]`, which is invalid JSON. The checkout handler parses this response
  before redirecting, so that parse failure silently killed the checkout button.
  A cart ending in a line with no metafield is exactly the standalone Insiders
  Club enrollment case, which is how it surfaced.

  The Club product carries no `productId` metafield of its own, so it is not
  forwarded. cc-cart.js.liquid handles the cart where that leaves the list empty.
{%- endcomment -%}
{
  "customer_logged_in": {% if customer %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
  "meta_product_id_array": [
    {%- assign first = true -%}
    {%- for item in cart.items -%}
      {%- if item.variant.metafields.productId.productId != blank -%}
        {%- unless first %},{% endunless -%}
        {
          "id": {{ item.variant.metafields.productId.productId | json }},
          "quantity": {{ item.quantity | json }}
        }
        {%- assign first = false -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
